# MAD vLLM patch for docker/vllm_disagg_inference.glmv5.3_quark_mxfp4_attnfp8.ubuntu.amd.Dockerfile
# What: MoRIIO registers kernel-block-split MLA/indexer KV views, needed for DSA models
#   (GlmMoeDsaForCausalLM) over MoRIIO when --block-size is neither 1 nor a multiple
#   of 16. At --block-size 16 (this recipe) the split path is not exercised.
# Upstream: vllm-project/vllm#60783 (open), squashed at 7d3b328165.
#   https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/60783
# Remove when: #60783 is merged and VLLM_REF contains it.
# ---- end of MAD header; the tested patch bytes follow unchanged ----
From 364da3408efea96f46c28bf1b3a0081dc4596e24 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mir Mustafa Ali <miali@amd.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 04:33:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] [Bugfix][KV Connector][ROCm] MoRIIO: accept
 kernel-block-split MLA/indexer KV views

If a backend's kernel block sizes exclude the manager block size,
create_kv_cache_views gives connectors a kernel-block-split 4-D view.
MoRIIO's 4-D branch only accepted r == 1, so registration failed with
"Unsupported MoRIIO MLA cache shape". ROCM_AITER_MLA_SPARSE and the DSA
indexer support kernel blocks [1, MultipleOf(16)], so DSA models
(GLM-5.2/5.3, DeepSeek-V3.2) hit this at --block-size 4 or 8.

Squashed from vllm-project/vllm#60783 (open) at 7d3b328165.
---
